// Which process a send reaches, over the targets the points-to stage
// resolved (processes.dl, staged by points_to.dl).
//
// Prerequisites: include clientlib/imports.dl and clientlib/otp.dl
// (which brings staged_processes.dl) before this file.

// The send at `id` in `func`, carrying `message`, may reach `proc`: the
// send's own target, or, when `func` sends to its parameter, whatever its
// callers hand it (process_call).
.decl send_target(id: symbol, func: symbol, message: symbol, proc: symbol)

send_target(id, f, m, p) :- pid_send(id, f, m, _, _), call_site_target(id, f, "info", p).

// The gen behaviours' own envelopes. A gen_server's loop takes a
// `{:"$gen_call", from, request}` to handle_call/3 and a
// `{:"$gen_cast", request}` to handle_cast/2 (a gen_statem's to its state
// function, as a call or a cast event), and a `{:system, from, request}`
// to :sys: none reaches handle_info/2, or an :info event. A library that
// sends one by hand — rabbit's gen_server2:cast/2 is `Dest ! {'$gen_cast',
// Request}` — makes a call or a cast. Spelled as pid_send spells a tuple
// by its tag.
// Read by tag and size, per send (send_envelope, PidFlow): the message
// spells a tuple by its tag alone, and `{:system, :reload}` is a message.
